course: dictionary
lesson: 12448
title: Taking away from a total
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To deduct something means to take an amount away from a total. It is a bit like subtract, but we often use deduct for money, points or tax. «Deduct 5 from 20» means start with 20 and take away 5, which leaves 15.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping in an easier word. «Deduct 5 from 20» becomes «subtract 5 from 20», and that still makes sense, so deduct means subtract here.
explain: In sport, «The referee deducted two points for the foul» means two points were taken away from the team's score. The team lost points, and the referee did not give any points away.
explain: Deduction is the noun. It means the amount that is taken away. If your pay has tax taken off, the tax is a deduction from your pay.
fact: Deduct means to take an amount away from a total.
fact: Deduct is a verb: deduct, deducts, deducted, deducting.
fact: Deduction is the noun for the amount taken away.
fact: «Deduct» is often used in maths, money and games.
fact: Subtract is a close synonym for deduct, but deduct is often used for money, points or tax.
exercise: «Deduct 5 from 20.» What does deduct mean here? | Multiply 20 by 5 | *Take 5 away from 20 | Add 5 to 20 | Share 20 into 5 equal parts
exercise: «The referee deducted two points for the foul.» What happened to the team's points? | The points stayed the same | Two points were given to them | *Two points were taken away from them | Two points were doubled
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to deduct? | Shout | Add | Guess | *Subtract
test: «Ella had 12 stickers and deducted 4 of them.» How many stickers does Ella have left? | 16 | 4 | 12 | *8
test: «Tax was deducted before Tom got his pay.» What happened to the tax? | It was given to his friend | *It was taken off the amount he was paid | It was added to his pay | It was paid twice
exam: Which sentence uses deduct correctly? | *Please deduct the cost from the total | Please deduct the wind from the door | Please deduct the song from the bird | Please deduct the colour from the sky
